#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:726
msgid "`cir.array.ctor` (::cir::ArrayCtor)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:728
msgid "_Initialize array elements with C++ constructors_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:739
msgid ""
"Initialize each array element using the same C++ constructor. This operation "
"has a `body` region and an optional `partial_dtor` region. Both regions have "
"a single block whose argument is a pointer to the current array element."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:744
msgid "The `body` region contains the constructor call for one element."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:746
msgid ""
"The `partial_dtor` region, when non-empty, contains the destructor call for "
"one element. During lowering, it is used to build a cleanup that destroys "
"already-constructed elements if a constructor throws. When the element type "
"has a trivial destructor or exceptions are disabled, the `partial_dtor` "
"region is left empty."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:752 ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:811
msgid ""
"When `num_elements` is absent, `addr` must be a pointer to a fixed-size CIR "
"array type and the element count is derived from that array type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:755
msgid ""
"When `num_elements` is present, `addr` is a pointer to the first element and "
"`num_elements` provides the runtime element count (for example `new T[n]`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:784 ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:845
msgid "Traits: `SingleBlockImplicitTerminator<cir::YieldOp>`, `SingleBlock`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:0
msgid "pointer type"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:0
msgid "`num_elements`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:795
msgid "`cir.array.dtor` (::cir::ArrayDtor)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:797
msgid "_Destroy array elements with C++ destructors_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:807
msgid ""
"Destroy each array element using the same C++ destructor. This operation has "
"one region with one block whose argument is a pointer to the current array "
"element."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:814
msgid ""
"When `num_elements` is present, `addr` is a pointer to the first element and "
"`num_elements` provides the runtime element count (e.g. from an array cookie "
"for `delete[]`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:818
msgid ""
"When `dtor_may_throw` is present, the element destructor call may throw an "
"exception."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:821
msgid "Elements are destroyed in reverse order."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:856
msgid "`cir.asin` (::cir::ASinOp)"
msgstr ""

