#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6022
msgid "`cir.fmaximum` (::cir::FMaximumOp)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6024
msgid "_Returns the larger of two floating-point values (IEEE 754-2019)_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6033
msgid ""
"`cir.fmaximum` returns the larger of its two operands according to IEEE "
"754-2019 semantics. If either operand is NaN, NaN is returned."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6062
msgid "`cir.fmaxnum` (::cir::FMaxNumOp)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6064
msgid "_Returns the larger of two floating-point values_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6073
msgid ""
"`cir.fmaxnum` returns the larger of its two operands. If one operand is NaN, "
"the other operand is returned."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6102
msgid "`cir.fminimum` (::cir::FMinimumOp)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6104
msgid "_Returns the smaller of two floating-point values (IEEE 754-2019)_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6113
msgid ""
"`cir.fminimum` returns the smaller of its two operands according to IEEE "
"754-2019 semantics. If either operand is NaN, NaN is returned."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6142
msgid "`cir.fminnum` (::cir::FMinNumOp)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6144
msgid "_Returns the smaller of two floating-point values_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6153
msgid ""
"`cir.fminnum` returns the smaller of its two operands. If one operand is "
"NaN, the other operand is returned."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6182
msgid "`cir.fmod` (::cir::FModOp)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6184
msgid "_Computes the floating-point remainder_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6193
msgid ""
"`cir.fmod` computes the floating-point remainder of dividing the first "
"operand by the second operand."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6222
msgid "`cir.fmul` (::cir::FMulOp)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6224
msgid "_Floating-point multiplication_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6232
msgid ""
"The `cir.fmul` operation performs floating-point multiplication on its "
"operands. Both operands and the result must have the same floating-point "
"scalar or vector-of-float type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6271
msgid "`cir.fmuladd` (::cir::FMulAddOp)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6273
msgid "_Contractable fused multiply-add operation_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6281
msgid ""
"Computes `(a * b) + c`, allowing the multiply and add to be fused (or not) "
"into a single rounding step at the target's discretion. It lowers to the "
"`llvm.fmuladd` intrinsic (or its constrained variant when an `fenv` "
"attribute is present)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6286
msgid ""
"Unlike `cir.fma`, which maps to `llvm.fma` and guarantees a single rounding, "
"`cir.fmuladd` expresses the FP-contraction relaxation used for `a * b + c` "
"under `-ffp-contract=on` / `fast`, where the backend is free to emit either "
"a fused or an unfused sequence."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6332
msgid "`cir.fneg` (::cir::FNegOp)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6334
msgid "_Floating-point negation_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6342
msgid ""
"The `cir.fneg` operation negates the operand. The operand and result must "
"have the same type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6345
msgid ""
"The optional `fastmath_flags` attribute holds the fast-math flags of the "
"operation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6364 ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:12349
#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:12388 ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:12426
