"<tr><td><code>fastmath_flags</code></td><td>::cir::FastMathFlagsAttr</"
"td><td>fast-math flags</td></tr>\n"
"</table>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6383
msgid "`cir.for` (::cir::ForOp)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6385
msgid "_C/C++ for loop counterpart_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6399
msgid "Represents a C/C++ for loop. It consists of three or four regions:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6401 ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:13363
msgid ""
"`cond`: single block region with the loop's condition. Should be terminated "
"with a `cir.condition` operation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6403 ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:13365
msgid "`body`: contains the loop body and an arbitrary number of blocks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6404
msgid "`step`: single block region with the loop's step."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6405
msgid ""
"`cleanup`: optional region that runs on every per-iteration exit edge "
"(condition-false exit, end-of-iteration after the step, break/continue, and "
"EH unwinding when the cleanup kind includes EH). This is used to destroy a "
"condition variable whose lifetime is a single iteration. When present, it "
"carries a cleanup kind matching `cir.cleanup.scope` (`normal` or `all`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6442 ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:13397
msgid ""
"<table>\n"
"<tr><th>Attribute</th><th>MLIR Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>\n"
"<tr><td><code>cleanupKind</code></td><td>::cir::CleanupKindAttr</"
"td><td>cleanup kind</td></tr>\n"
"<tr><td><code>loop_id</code></td><td>::mlir::DistinctAttr</td><td>distinct "
"attribute</td></tr>\n"
"<tr><td><code>loop_hints</code></td><td>::cir::LoopHintAttr</"
"td><td>Optimizer hints and guarantees attached to a loop</td></tr>\n"
"</table>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6451
msgid "`cir.frame_address` (::cir::FrameAddrOp)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6453
msgid "_The frame address of the current function, or of one of its callers_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6461
msgid ""
"Represents a call to builtin function ` __builtin_frame_address` in CIR. "
"This builtin function returns the frame address of the current function, or "
"of one of its callers. The frame is the area on the stack that holds local "
"variables and saved registers. The frame address is normally the address of "
"the first word pushed on to the stack by the function. However, the exact "
"definition depends upon the processor and the calling convention. If the "
"processor has a dedicated frame pointer register, and the function has a "
"frame, then __builtin_frame_address returns the value of the frame pointer "
"register."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6471
msgid ""
"The `level` argument is number of frames to scan up the call stack. For "
"instance, value of 0 yields the frame address of the current function, value "
"of 1 yields the frame address of the caller of the current function, and so "
"forth."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:0
msgid "`level`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6496
msgid "`cir.freeze` (::cir::FreezeOp)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6498
msgid "_Stop propagation of undef and poison values_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6506
msgid ""
"The `cir.freeze` operation takes a single operand and returns a value of the "
"same type. If the operand is a poison or undef value, `cir.freeze` returns "
"an arbitrary, but fixed, value of the operand type. Otherwise it returns the "
"operand unchanged."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6537
msgid "`cir.frem` (::cir::FRemOp)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6539
msgid "_Floating-point remainder_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6547
msgid ""
"The `cir.frem` operation computes the floating-point remainder of its "
"operands. Both operands and the result must have the same floating-point "
"scalar or vector-of-float type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6586
msgid "`cir.frexp` (::cir::FrexpOp)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6588
msgid "_Decomposes a floating-point value into significand and exponent_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6596
msgid ""
"`cir.frexp` splits a floating-point value into a normalized significand (in "
"the range [0.5, 1.0)) and an integral power-of-two exponent, such that `src "
"= significand * 2^exp`.  Returns both as separate results."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6600
msgid "Lowers to `llvm.frexp`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:0
msgid "`exp`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6626
msgid "`cir.fshl` (::cir::FshlOp)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6628
msgid "_Funnel shift left_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6636
msgid ""
"The `cir.fshl` operation concatenates `a` and `b` (with `a` in the high "
"half), shifts the concatenation left by `c` bit positions, and returns the "
"high half of the result. The shift amount is treated modulo the bitwidth of "
"the operands."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6641 ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6688
msgid ""
"All operands and the result must have the same integer type or vector-of-"
"integer type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6673
msgid "`cir.fshr` (::cir::FshrOp)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6675
msgid "_Funnel shift right_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6683
msgid ""
"The `cir.fshr` operation concatenates `a` and `b` (with `a` in the high "
"half), shifts the concatenation right by `c` bit positions, and returns the "
"low half of the result. The shift amount is treated modulo the bitwidth of "
"the operands."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6720
msgid "`cir.fsub` (::cir::FSubOp)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6722
msgid "_Floating-point subtraction_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6730
msgid ""
"The `cir.fsub` operation performs floating-point subtraction on its "
"operands. Both operands and the result must have the same floating-point "
"scalar vector-of-float or matrix-of-float type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6771
msgid "`cir.func` (::cir::FuncOp)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6773
msgid "_Declare or define a function_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6775
msgid ""
"The `cir.func` operation defines a function, similar to the `mlir::FuncOp` "
"built-in."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6778
msgid ""
"The function linkage information is specified by `linkage`, as defined by "
"`GlobalLinkageKind` attribute."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6781
msgid ""
"The `calling_conv` attribute specifies the calling convention of the "
"function. By default calling convention is `CallingConv::C`. When printed, C "
"calling convention is omitted. Other calling conventions are printed as "
"`cc(<mnemonic>)`, e.g. `cc(amdgpu_kernel)`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6786
msgid ""
"A compiler builtin function must be marked as `builtin` for further "
"processing when lowering from CIR."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6789
msgid ""
"The `coroutine` keyword is used to mark a coroutine function, which requires "
"at least one `cir.await` instruction to be used in its body."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6792
msgid ""
"The `lambda` translates to a C++ `operator()` that implements a lambda, this "
"allow callsites to make certain assumptions about the real function nature "
"when writing analysis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6796
msgid ""
"The `no_proto` keyword is used to identify functions that were declared "
"without a prototype and, consequently, may contain calls with invalid "
"arguments and undefined behavior."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6800
msgid ""
"The `requires_call_conv_lowering` keyword marks a function whose signature "
"and call sites still have to be rewritten to match the target ABI by "
"CallConvLowering. Every function built in C++ starts out with it, and the "
"pass drops it once the function is lowered. A lowered signature uses "
"ordinary CIR types and cannot be told apart from one that still needs "
"lowering, so the pass works only on functions that carry the keyword."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6807
msgid ""
"The `global_ctor` keyword indicates whether a function should execute before "
"`main()` function, as specified by `__attribute__((constructor))`. An "
"execution priority can also be specified `global_ctor(<priority>)`. "
"Similarly, for global destructors both `global_dtor` and "
"`global_dtor(<priority>)` are available."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6813
msgid ""
"The `no_inline` attribute marks a function that should not be inlined. The "
"`always_inline` attribute marks a function that should always be inlined. "
"The `inline_hint` attribute suggests that the function should be inlined."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6817
msgid ""
"The `personality` attribute specifies the personality function to use for "
"exception handling. This is a symbol reference to the personality function "
"(e.g., `@__gxx_personality_v0` for C++ exceptions)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6821
msgid ""
"The 'comdat' attribute marks the function as belonging to a COMDAT group. "
"This attribute includes an optional 'group' name, which if not provided, "
"results in the function's symbol name being used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6857
msgid ""
"Traits: `AutomaticAllocationScope`, `IsolatedFromAbove`, `SymbolName`, "
"`SymbolVisibility`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6859
msgid ""
"Interfaces: `ArgAndResultAttrsOpInterface`, `CIRGlobalValueInterface`, "
"`CallableOpInterface`, `FunctionOpInterface`, `Symbol`"
msgstr ""

