#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7976
msgid "`cir.libc.memchr` (::cir::MemChrOp)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7978
msgid "_Libc's `memchr`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7988
msgid ""
"Search for `pattern` in data range from `src` to `src` + `len`. `len` "
"provides a bound to the search in `src`. `result` is a pointer to found "
"`pattern` or a null pointer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7992
msgid ""
"`pattern` has the width of the target int and `len` has the width of the "
"target size_t. The module records these widths as `cir.int_type_width` and "
"`cir.size_type_width`, each a signless i32 holding a fundamental integer "
"width, and the verifier checks the operands against them. `src` must be a "
"void pointer in the default address space and `result` has the same type as "
"`src`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:0
msgid "`pattern`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:0
msgid "fundamental signed integer type"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:0
msgid "`len`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:8023
msgid "`cir.libc.memcpy` (::cir::MemCpyOp)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:8025
msgid "_Equivalent to libc's `memcpy`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:8035
msgid ""
"Given two CIR pointers, `src` and `dst`, `cir.libc.memcpy` will copy `len` "
"bytes from the memory pointed by `src` to the memory pointed by `dst`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:8038
msgid ""
"While `cir.copy` is meant to be used for implicit copies in the code where "
"the length of the copy is known, `cir.memcpy` copies only from and to void "
"pointers, requiring the copy length to be passed as an argument."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:8042
msgid ""
"As is the case for memcpy in the C standard library, this operation exhibits "
"undefined behavior (UB) if any of the following conditions hold:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:8044
msgid "`src` and/or `dst` are null pointers; or"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:8045
