#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:11442
msgid "`cir.trap` (::cir::TrapOp)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:11444
msgid "_Exit the program abnormally_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:11452
msgid ""
"The cir.trap operation causes the program to exit abnormally. The "
"implementations may implement this operation with different mechanisms. For "
"example, an implementation may implement this operation by calling abort, "
"while another implementation may implement this operation by executing an "
"illegal instruction."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:11458
msgid ""
"The `implicit` keyword marks a trap that CIRGen synthesized because control "
"flows off the end of a non-void function body."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:11465 ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:11770
msgid ""
