msgid "`cir.vtable.get_entry` (::cir::VTableGetEntryOp)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:12959
msgid "_Get a pointer entry from a vtable_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:12968
msgid ""
"The `vtable.get_entry` operation reads an entry of an object's vtable that "
"holds a pointer, other than a virtual function. This is an ABI independent "
"abstraction of this operation: how the entry is stored and read is decided "
"when the operation is lowered."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:12973 ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:13028
msgid ""
"The `vptr` operand must be a `!cir.vptr` value, which would have been "
"returned by a previous call to `cir.vtable.get_vptr`. The `index` operand is "
"the index of the entry in the vtable, counted from the address point. "
"Entries that precede the address point have a negative index."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:12978
msgid "The result is the pointer that the entry holds."
msgstr ""

