#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:13024
msgid ""
"The `vtable.get_offset` operation reads an offset that is stored in an "
"object's vtable, such as the offset of a virtual base class or a virtual "
"adjustment for a thunk, in an ABI independent way."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:13033
msgid "The result is the value of the offset, in bytes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:13067
msgid "`cir.vtable.get_type_info` (::cir::VTableGetTypeInfoOp)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:13069
msgid "_Get the type_info of an object from its vtable_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:13077
msgid ""
"The `vtable.get_type_info` operation retrieves the pointer to the dynamic "
"type_info/rtti object from an object's vtable (__vptr). This is an ABI "
"independent abstraction of this operation: where the entry is, and how it is "
"stored and read, is decided when the operation is lowered."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:13082 ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:13194
msgid ""
"The `vptr` operand must be a `!cir.vptr` value, which would have been "
"returned by a previous call to `cir.vtable.get_vptr`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:13085
msgid "The result is the pointer to the `type_info` struct."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:13112
msgid "`cir.vtable.get_virtual_fn` (::cir::VTableGetVirtualFnOp)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:13114
msgid "_Get a virtual function pointer from a vtable_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:13123
msgid ""
"The `vtable.get_virtual_fn` operation retrieves the pointer to a virtual "
"function from an object's vtable (__vptr). This is an ABI independent "
"abstraction of this operation: how the entry is stored and read is decided "
"when the operation is lowered."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:13128
msgid ""
"The `vptr` operand must be a `!cir.vptr` value, which would have been "
"returned by a previous call to `cir.vtable.get_vptr`. The `index` operand is "
"the index of the virtual function in the vtable, counted from the address "
"point."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:13133
msgid ""
"The `invariant` attribute marks that the entry does not change for as long "
"as the vtable is live, which allows the load of it to be optimized."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:13136 ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:13197
msgid "The result is the pointer to the function."
