msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:13177
msgid "_Get a virtual function pointer from a vtable by its offset_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:13186
msgid ""
"The `vtable.get_virtual_fn_by_offset` operation is the counterpart of "
"`cir.vtable.get_virtual_fn` for when the entry is only known at run time, "
"such as when calling through a pointer to member function. The entry is "
"identified by its `offset` operand, which is the distance in bytes of the "
"entry from the address point of the vtable, as it is stored in the pointer "
"to member function. How the entry is stored and read is decided when the "
"operation is lowered."
