msgid "_CIR exception handling token type_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16617
msgid "Syntax: `!cir.eh_token`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16619
msgid ""
"`!cir.eh_token` is an opaque type used to track exception handling state in "
"flattened CIR. It is returned by `cir.eh.initiate` and passed to "
"`cir.eh.dispatch`, `cir.begin_cleanup`, and `cir.begin_catch` operations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16623
msgid ""
"This token represents an in-flight exception and is used during ABI-lowering "
"to generate the appropriate exception handling code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16627
msgid "FP16Type"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16629
msgid "_CIR half-precision 16-bit float type_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16631
msgid "Syntax: `!cir.f16`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16633
msgid ""
"A 16-bit floating-point type whose format is IEEE-754 `binary16`. It "
"represents the types '_Float16` and `std::float16_t` in C and C++."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16637
